  "note": "Triennial election of 15 January 1923, the first after proportional representation was abolished; Portadown was divided into three wards (North 5 seats, South-East 4, South-West 6) by a Ministry of Home Affairs order of 31 October 1922 (Belfast Gazette, 10 November 1922). Messrs Campbell, Copeland, Corbett, Locke, Moffett, G. Johnston, W. J. Johnston and Mrs M'Cammon were the official nominees of the Labour Unionist Association; \"all the other candidates were Independent Unionists\". Counted 16 January. North Ward: Copeland, a retiring member, was the only Labour Unionist nominee defeated."
